<title>UK: Speciality Shops buys shopping centre.</title>
<headline>Speciality Shops buys shopping centre.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Property investment company Speciality Shops Plc said on Thursday it had purchased the freehold interest of the The Pyramids Shopping centre in Birkenhead for 26.75 million stg.</p>
<p>The property was bought from Wyndham Investments, the property arm of the Allied Domecq Pension Fund.  </p>
<p>The property would show an initial return of 8.25 percent on the current income of 2.25 million stg, Speciality said.</p>
<p>Speciality said its 1996 group assets more than doubled to 110 million stg with its net asset value per share estimated to have increased to 1.45 stg from 1.34 stg.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
